\DOC mk_genvar

\TYPE {mk_genvar : int * hol_type -> term}

\SYNOPSIS
Constructs a variable named like those of genvars with a given number.

\DESCRIBE
The call {mk_genvar(n,ty)} returns the variable of type {ty} named {_v}
followed by the number {n}, the names that {genvars} gives. These names are
never given by {genvar}, whose names are an underscore followed by a number.

\FAILURE
Never fails.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # mk_genvar(5,`:bool`);;
  val it : term = `_v5`
}

\SEEALSO
genvar, genvar_index, genvars, mk_var.

\ENDDOC
